WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.090 --> 00:00:07.349 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  i'm talina kopien i'm co-founder of  purse rehab we're a family-owned company  we've been in business for 35 years i'm  going to walk you through how my team  restores a 2 000  louis vuitton belt back that's been  slashed it's from their 2003 collection  so it's discontinued our client reached  out to us unfortunately this was part of  an argument with an ex-boyfriend who  decided to slash her favorite bag  the repair process will entail several  steps  what we have here is our senior  technician disassembling the front  pocket of the bag from the main zipper  compartment and this is done by undoing  the stitching that's on the outermost  layer  and what we're using here is a round awl  to open up the stitches it's important  to use a round awl because this will  help with not damaging the canvas  once we've taken apart the front pocket  we will move on to the main lining and  we will undo the stitching there to  remove the piping which is basically  what's keeping the front pocket and the  main compartment together and again we  will be using the same round all to do  this step  once we're done with the deconstruction  phase we will be replacing the following  pieces that have the most damage the  front pocket which includes the lining  and the lining that is also part of the  main compartment which is outer facing  so the three layers will be replaced  here we're recreating the pieces that  we're going to replace and we do this by  making templates to match the exact size  of the original piece that we're  replacing we're using a sharp knife to  cut out the template we have three  different pieces that we'll be doing so  this is an important part of the  replacement process to ensure that we  get the exact same template that matches  the original piece  we are using authentic recycled louis  vuitton material we have the canvas that  we'll be replacing with an authentic  piece that matches the original and we  are also using the lining from a  recycled bag that matches the existing  lining  so in essence we are using the exact  same type of material to restore the  pieces that we are replacing  here our senior technician is skiving  the canvas  skiving is a process where the leather  or canvas is thinned out it's  essentially shaved to a thinner layer  and it's typically only done around the  edges because those are the areas that  we're going to fold and stitch  once the canvas is skived our technician  here is applying glue to the area that  was skived and we're using a plastic  container with a pointy tip to ensure  that the glue is only applied to the  area that we need to apply to  [Music]  we have applied the glue now we'll be  putting the lining together with the  canvas that we recreated and we apply  the heat because the heat helps activate  the glue so that it adheres better and  it's secure  once we've completed this step we're  going to stitch the louis vuitton  monogram piece that we are reusing this  is the original piece  that we're restitching on the lining  that we cut out so the lining is new but  the top portion is the existing piece  so once we restitch this together  we will bring the front pocket and the  back lining  together once the two pieces have been  separately stitched  we will glue them together using contact  cement glue we need to glue every piece  before we do the stitching to ensure  there's no movement  and it's very secure  and once we have the front pocket and  the back lining together we are going to  put in the date code this is an  important piece to retain the  authenticity of the bag  once that's done the next step is to  re-glue the piping to the trim of the  front pocket again here we're reusing  the same piping  because it wasn't damaged and we want to  retain as much of the original parts as  possible  after gluing the piping we're going to  restitch to the front pocket you'll  notice that the piping has two stitch  lines one is to stitch the piping to the  front pocket and the second line is to  stitch it to the main compartment  the next step here is to patch up the  interior lining cut we did not replace  the full interior lining in an effort to  retain the original pieces because it  wasn't very damaged and it's a less  visible space we're using a wider brush  to apply the glue because we're working  with wider space so we don't have to be  as precise  we're now gluing the main compartment to  the exterior pocket  and we are stapling the two pieces  together this is not something that's  typically done in this industry but our  senior technician has been using this  technique for many years and it's a  successful technique because it's  basically an added layer of security to  ensure that there's zero movement when  we're stitching all the pieces together  and he's hammering down the staples to  ensure that they're flat and there's no  chance of them being caught in the  sewing machine when we do the stitching  and we're using a guide to ensure that  the stitching is straight and aligned  with the bag  and here we are removing the staples  using a stapler remover and this is a  rounded tip so it doesn't cause any  damage to the bag  we're hammering the edges of the bag  after turning it right side out to  straighten out the edges and ensure  everything is in place  of course we have to straighten out the  piping to make sure everything is in  place so that the final stitching will  be as perfect as possible  we have to be very careful in this  particular stage to ensure that the  needles  go back into the same hole so we have to  be very focused and very careful in  making sure that we are using not only  the same color thread the thickness of  the thread has to match and we follow  the holes accordingly  i'm super pleased with the results and  so proud of our team and our senior  technician for taking this challenge on  and giving this bag a second life i  can't wait to share it with our client  [Music]

